      "description": "Watch Newells Old Boys vs Boca Juniors highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 2, 2026. The stage was set for a classic encounter in the Liga Profesional Argentina , as two historic rivals faced off in a match brimming with tactical intrigue and raw emotion. Fans expected a battle, and the players delivered a spectacle that showcased the unpredictable nature of South American football. Boca Juniors Take the Initiative On August 2, 2026 , the opening exchanges were defined by high pressing and physical duels. Boca Juniors found the breakthrough in the 30th minute when Sebastian Villa turned provider, setting up Santiago Ascacibar for a clinical finish. The goal gave the visitors a platform to build on, though the physical cost was evident as Lautaro Giannetti and Ayrton Costa both entered the referee's book before the halftime whistle blew. Newell's Strike Back with Purpose The second half saw a dramatic shift in momentum as Newell's Old Boys emerged with renewed vigor. Just five minutes after the restart, Matias Coccaro leveled the scores following a clever assist from Facundo Samuel Guch . The momentum stayed with the home side, and in the 59th minute, Luca Regiardo —who had been cautioned just moments earlier—capitalized on a Lautaro Rios pass to complete the comeback and put Newell's in the driving seat. Late Drama and a Shared Result As the clock ticked down, Boca Juniors threw everything forward in search of an equalizer. The defining moment arrived in the 81st minute. Alan Velasco , despite having just received a yellow card, kept his composure to convert a chance created by Tomas Aranda . The final minutes were a frantic affair with multiple substitutions and 11 minutes of added time, but neither side could find a winner, leaving the points shared after a breathtaking contest."
