      "description": "Watch Deportivo Riestra vs Boca Juniors highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 27, 2026. The Liga Profesional Argentina delivered a high-stakes encounter on July 27, 2026, as Deportivo Riestra played host to the legendary Boca Juniors . Both sides took to the pitch with clear strategic intentions, creating an electric atmosphere for the fans in attendance. First-Half Dominance Deportivo Riestra wasted no time in asserting their authority, launching a relentless offensive display from the opening whistle. The deadlock was broken just 7 minutes into the match when Antony Alonso turned provider, setting up Brian Sanchez for a clinical finish that sent the home crowd into raptures. Boca Juniors struggled to find their rhythm as the hosts continued to exploit gaps in the defensive line. The pressure told again in the 23rd minute. This time, Carlos Quintana delivered a precise ball to Antony Alonso , who followed up his earlier assist with a well-taken goal of his own. Riestra’s clinical nature was on full display, and they further punished a shell-shocked Boca defense in the 38th minute. Alexander Diaz found the target to make it three, capping off a remarkable first-half performance that left the visitors with a mountain to climb. Strategic Resilience and Final Whistle At the start of the second half, Boca Juniors attempted to spark a comeback by introducing Angel Romero and Sebastian Villa from the bench. While the tactical shifts brought more possession for the visitors, Deportivo Riestra remained disciplined and compact. Substitutions for the home side, including Nicolas Benegas and Jonatan Goitia , helped maintain their energy levels as they focused on game management. As the match entered its closing stages, the intensity rose, leading to several bookings. Milton Aaron Celiz , Jonatan Goitia , and Nicolas Watson all saw yellow cards as Riestra fought to protect their lead. Despite late pressure and further changes from Boca, including the introduction of Miguel Merentiel , the hosts held firm. The final whistle after 94 minutes confirmed a significant victory for Riestra, built on the foundations of their devastating first-half blitz."
